# a drum step's two strengths on its key: an empty step is set strong (100); pressed again, soft (64);
# again, off. A hit of any velocity over 82 goes to soft, one at 82 or under off; turning a knob while
# held keeps it as turned
wait 200
expect track 0
expect step1 0
tapkey w1
wait 20
expect step1 1
expect vel1 100
tapkey w1
wait 20
expect step1 1
expect vel1 64
tapkey w1
wait 20
expect step1 0
# set, then held and turned up to 127: it stays at 127
tapkey w1
wait 20
key w1 down
wait 20
spin K1 40
key w1 up
wait 20
expect step1 1
expect vel1 127
tapkey w1
wait 20
expect vel1 64
# held and turned down (to 44): let go, it stays; pressed, it goes
key w1 down
wait 20
spin K1 -5
key w1 up
wait 20
expect vel1 44
tapkey w1
wait 20
expect step1 0
expect dropped 0
